= Overview =

This document describes the procedure to enable SSL connection between PKI server and the internal database.

There are several scenarios:
* [https://www.dogtagpki.org/wiki/Enabling_SSL_Connection_with_Internal_Database_on_New_Instance Enabling SSL Connection with Internal Database on New Instance]
* [https://www.dogtagpki.org/wiki/Enabling_SSL_Connection_with_Internal_Database_on_Existing_Instance Enabling SSL Connection with Internal Database on Existing Instance]
* [https://github.com/dogtagpki/pki/wiki/Enabling-Secure-Connection-to-Internal-Database Enabling Secure Connection to Internal Database]

Once the SSL is enabled, see the following page to enable client certificate authentication:
* [https://github.com/dogtagpki/pki/wiki/Configuring-Client-Certificate-Authentication-to-Internal-Database Configuring Client Certificate Authentication to Internal Database]

